# Third-party licenses

SAIFE Sandbox contains third-party code. This file lists every dependency that is
compiled into the shipped `saife.exe` / `saife-launch.exe` binaries, grouped by
license, with the full license text and the copyright holders the licenses ask
to be named. The MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, Unlicense and Unicode-3.0 licenses
all require this text to be reproduced in every distribution of the binary.

The file is generated from `Cargo.lock` by
[cargo-about](https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-about) with the
configuration in `packaging/licenses/`. Do not edit it by hand; regenerate it
with `packaging/licenses/generate.ps1`.

Where a licence expression offers a choice (for example `MIT OR Apache-2.0`),
the text reproduced below is the one `accepted` in `about.toml` selects first.
No dependency is licensed under a copyleft licence.

